        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Surrealism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> was the most important centre; autonomous groups in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, a second English group in Birmingham, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chile">Chile</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and Martinique; from the 1930s the idea spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and Asia, and in the 1940s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> became a place of exile</span></div>
